=== CTL-2  DECODE goes RED where ALIGN stays GREEN ==========
# C10's addr moved to a DIFFERENT REAL instruction boundary in the SAME
# function (0x10b60a25, 'mov eax,[edi+0x4c]'). This is exactly the C10/C15
# defect class: aligned, right function, wrong instruction. ALIGN cannot
# see it; DECODE is the only check that can.
$ python3 work/w-inlmetric/check_table.py --plant C10=10b60a25
table    : work/w-inlmetric/CLAUSES.tsv
rows     : 24
  state    : {'absent': 17, 'fitted': 2, 'R-derived': 2, 'unexercisable': 3}
  exercised: {'yes': 9, 'not-separable': 6, 'no': 6, 'unexercisable': 3}
listing  : ~/ghidra-projects/export/c2/objdump_intel.asm
  ALIGN  : 424,232 instruction starts, 24 of 24 rows graded
  DECODE : 24 of 24 rows carry an `asm` cell and were graded
planted  : {'C10': '10b60a25'}
  FAIL C10(PLANTED): DECODE 0x10b60a25 is 'mov eax,DWORD PTR [edi+0x4c]', table records 'and eax,0x2000'

CONFORMANCE-CHECK: RED  (1 failure(s) over 24 rows)
exit=1

